welcome back to the david pakman show i  am fair and cousins sitting in for david  pakman today and don't forget you can  follow me on twitter in fact on all  social media at farren balanced you can  also get me on youtube.com  fair and balanced and the big youtube  channel youtube.com slash the ring of  fire  well folks we've done a good job today  so far of not  talking about donald trump  so let's talk about donald trump right  now because there has been some some  trump developments this week uh the  first thing i want to talk about here  there was a piece this week from a good  friend of mine at salon.com writer by  the name of chauncey de vega  a piece titled are trump's followers  being conned  no  they gave him 100 million because they  love him  if you have a chance i encourage  everybody go read this piece because i  love it  see for a long time  many many years actually  i have been saying that trump is conning  his supporters  so when i saw this piece i almost felt  like oh oh no i hope i'm not mentioned  in it because i've had mentioned they'd  be were being conned even earlier this  week when it was reported that donald  trump had a hundred million dollars  a hundred million dollars that he is  definitely not using to help his good  friend rudy giuliani but that's a story  for a different day that david actually  covered earlier this week  either way trump's got a hundred million  dollars  he's raising it from all over the  country people just sending him money  money money  he's spending it at his own properties  to a degree hundreds of thousands of  dollars have been spent on his own  properties which he has a hundred  percent interest in some of the  properties where it's been spent so most  of it goes right back into his own  pocket  so  my logical conclusion is yes these  individuals are being conned because  some of this money a good chunk of it  was raised under the guise of we're  going to use this the trump pacs were  going to use this  to pay for ballot audits to pay for  election challenges  and they spent a whopping zero dollars  on it  so they gave trump money  thinking it was going to one thing and  then it didn't go to that  and i you know would come to the  conclusion logically  these people are being conned  but chauncey de vega actually makes a  much better point  than i was able to make  and he says  it's not that they're being conned  sure they might be being conned but they  also don't care they would still give  the money to him regardless  and there's a great explanation as to  why  see we found out late last year  that the trump campaign was essentially  and the rnc did it i think a little bit  too but anyway they were essentially  scamming their supporters and auto  enrolling them in these monthly  donations  so somebody thought they're giving a  one-time donation they didn't read the  fine print they didn't go through all  the you know hurdles  to turn off the recurring payment  and so they just kept month after month  after month some people lost you know  tons and tons of money for this  and even after they turned it off though  some of them are still giving money to  donald trump  they said oh yeah it was horrible we got  swindled here  i was thinking of giving money  and that's just one  example that you know kind of proves the  point that  they don't care that they're being  conned  and that's a point that the vega really  makes very well in this piece is that  even if the money doesn't go  where they think it's going to go  even if they're told one thing and a  completely opposite thing happens  they still like him  they still want him to be the president  they still support him they are still  going to give him  that money  now i had actually mentioned in a  segment on my channel fair balance  earlier this week  that i've run out of sympathy for these  people i have no more empathy  if they go bankrupt giving money to  donald trump  sure i don't want it to happen but at  this point they've had enough warnings  that if it happens it happens  because  it's worse than being conned  and that's kind of the point that the  vega makes in the piece you know that  that's that's the big  conclusion here is that it's worse than  a con  it's a cult  that's what it is it doesn't matter what  he does to some of these people  again i'm not saying all republicans are  in the cult but you do have this  die-hard sect of trump supporters that  it is really difficult to describe them  as anything else because it doesn't  matter what he says it doesn't matter  what he does it doesn't matter if he  lies to their face about it heck we got  reports that he likely didn't donate the  last couple  months of his salary like he promised to  always do and his kids would always  boast about on social media  we also know that gdp growth under  donald trump this another story came out  this week  was the lowest it's ever been since the  great depression  no president had worse gdp growth than  donald trump george w bush came close  his was 1.8 percent over eight years  trump's was 1.6 over four years so  economically speaking the guy was really  really bad  but the supporters don't care  they're still clamoring for him they  still want more from him they still want  him to be president again  probably holding out hope that what is  this a week from august 13th at this  point oh my god  you know if lindell's original  correction was correct or prediction was  correct excuse me we'd be a week away  from trump coming back and these people  would love it they don't care about the  lies they don't care about the vulgar  behavior they don't care about how he  mocked a disabled reporter way back in  the day they don't care about any of it  and they don't care what he uses their  money for  they just want to keep giving it to him  and at this point those individuals  it's likely that they can't be pulled  out of this certainly not by somebody  like me  you know you would need somebody who  actually understands that kind of cult  mentality and how to actually deprogram  people  which yes there are experts in that  and those are the ones who really would  have to work on these individuals  but until then they're going to keep  giving until they can't give any more  they know they're being conned  they just stopped caring
 

